          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The Elvis operator is a shortening of the ternary operator syntax and is used in the "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Groovy"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "link",
            "target": "https://www.groovy-lang.org/operators.html#_elvis_operator"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " language. With the ternary operator syntax, you usually have to repeat a variable twice, as the following example shows:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "String name = \"Elvis Presley\";\nString displayName = (name != null ? name : \"Unknown\");"
          }
        ],
        "language": "groovy",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Instead, you can use the Elvis operator (named for the resemblance to Elvis' hair style). The following example shows how to use the Elvis operator:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
